  "section" : {
    "accno" : "s-E-MTAB-14917",
    "type" : "Study",
    "attributes" : [ {
      "name" : "Title",
      "value" : "Age- and ApoE genotype-dependent transcriptomic responses to O3 in the hippocampus of mice"
    }, {
      "name" : "Study type",
      "value" : "RNA-seq of coding RNA",
      "valqual" : [ {
        "name" : "Ontology",
        "value" : "EFO"
      }, {
        "name" : "TermId",
        "value" : "EFO_0003738"
      } ]
    }, {
      "name" : "Organism",
      "value" : "Mus musculus"
    }, {
      "name" : "Description",
      "value" : "We earlier demonstrated that ozone an urban pollutant, accelerates AD-like neuropathology in aging male ApoE3 mice. In this study, we investigate hippocampal transcriptomic alterations in young and aged E3 and E4 mice following O₃ exposure to elucidate the molecular mechanisms underlying O₃-induced AD pathology specifically in old E3 male mice."
    } ],
    "links" : [ [ {
      "url" : "ERP170080",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "ENA"
      } ]
    } ] ],
    "subsections" : [ [ {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-151812",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-151812"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "sample collection protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0005518"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "Mice were euthanized by isoflurane overdose followed by bilateral thoracotomy. Brains were dissected sagittally into right and left hemispheres. The right hemisphere was fixed in 10% phosphate-buffered formalin, while the left hemisphere was dissected to isolate the hippocampus and cerebral cortex, which were snap-frozen in liquid nitrogen."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-151813",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-151813"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "nucleic acid extraction protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0002944"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "Total RNA was extracted from the hippocampus using TRIzol reagent (Invitrogen; Ther-mo Fisher Scientific, Inc.) [59]. RNA concentration and purity were measured using a NanoDrop ND-1000 spectrophotometer (NanoDrop Technologies, Wilmington, DE, USA), and RNA integrity was evaluated using the RNA Nano 6000 Assay Kit on the Agilent Bi-oanalyzer 2100 system (Agilent Technologies, CA, USA)."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-151814",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-151814"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "nucleic acid library construction protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0004184"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "A total of 1 µg RNA per sample was used for library preparation using the NEB-Next® Ultra™ RNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina® (NEB, USA) according to the manu-facturer’s protocol. mRNA was purified using poly-T oligo-attached magnetic beads, fragmented under elevated temperature, and reverse transcribed into cDNA using random hexamer primers. The second-strand cDNA was synthesized using DNA polymerase I and RNase H, followed by end repair, adaptor ligation, and size selection (150–200 bp). Amplified libraries were purified and quality-checked using the Agilent Bioanalyzer 2100."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware",
        "value" : "Illumina® (NEB, USA)"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-151815",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-151815"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "nucleic acid sequencing protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0004170"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "The sequencing libraries were clustered on the Illumina NovaSeq platform using paired-end sequencing to generate high-quality reads for each sample"
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware",
        "value" : "Illumina NovaSeq X"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-151816",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-151816"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "growth protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0003789"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "Three-month-old (3M) and seventeen-month-old (17M) male human E4 and E3 gene targeted replacement (TR) mice were obtained from Taconic and housed at the University of Alabama at Birmingham (UAB)."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-151817",
      "type" : "Protocols",
      "attributes" : [ {
        "name" : "Name",
        "value" : "P-MTAB-151817"
      }, {
        "name" : "Type",
        "value" : "treatment protocol",
        "valqual" : [ {
          "name" : "Ontology",
          "value" : "EFO"
        }, {
          "name" : "TermId",
          "value" : "EFO_0003969"
        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "Mice were subjected to either eight cycles of O₃ exposure or filtered air (FA) at the UAB environmental exposure facility. Each cycle consisted of 5 days of FA/O₃ exposure (0.8 ppm), for 7 hours per day followed by 9 days of FA. A total of 14 to 16 mice were used per genotype, age, and treatment group."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware"
      } ]
    }, {
      "accno" : "P-MTAB-151818",
      "type" : "Protocols",
